<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Comparing population growth of forest A and B</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>For each \(t\), the population of a forest is represented by the function \( \displaystyle A(t)={@initial_A@}({@baseA@})^{t}\). In a neighboring forest, the population of the same type of trees is represented by the function \(\displaystyle B(t) = {@initial_B@}({@baseB@})^t\).</p>

	<ol type ="a">
    	<li>
        	<p>Which forest's population is growing at a faster rate?</p>
                <p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
    	</li>

    	<li>
        	<p>Which forest had a greater number of trees initially? By how many? Take \(t=0\)</p>
                <p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
    	</li>

    	<li>
        	<p>Assuming the population growth models continue to represent the growth of the forests, which forest will have a greater number of trees after {@years@} years? By how many?</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> Give your answer rounded to the nearest whole number where necessary</p>
        	            <p>Evaluate \(A(t)\) and \(B(t)\) at \(t = {@years@}\):</p>
            <ol type="i">
                <li>
                    <p>For forest \(A\):</p>
                    <p>\( A({@years@}) =\)  [[input:ans3a]] \(\text{trees}\) [[validation:ans3a]] [[feedback:prt3a]]</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>For forest \(B\):</p>
                    <p>\( B({@years@}) =\)  [[input:ans3b]] \(\text{trees}\) [[validation:ans3b]] [[feedback:prt3b]]</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>The difference is:  [[input:ans3c]] \(\text{trees}\) [[validation:ans3c]] [[feedback:prt3c]]</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>Which forest will have a greater number of trees after {@years@} years?</p>
                    <p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>
                </li>
            </ol>
    	</li>
	</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Forest A:  \( \displaystyle A(t)={@initial_A@}({@baseA@})^{t}\)</p>
<p>Forest B:  \( \displaystyle B(t)={@initial_B@}({@baseB@})^{t}\)</p>

	<ol type ="a">
    	<li>
        	<p>Which forest's population is growing at a faster rate?</p>
 <p>To compare the growth rates of the populations in the two forests, we consider the bases of the exponential functions:</p>
            <p>For forest \(A\), the growth rate is determined by the base \({@baseA@}\), raised to the power \(t\).</p>
            <p>For forest \(B\), the growth rate is given directly by the base \({@baseB@}\).</p>
            <p>Comparing the growth rates \({@baseA@}\) (for forest \(A\)) and \({@baseB@}\) (for forest \(B\)),</p>
                <p>We see that, <strong> {@effective_growth@}</strong></p>
    	</li>

    	<li>
        	<p>Which forest had a greater number of trees initially? By how many? Take \(t=0\)</p>
 <p>The initial number of trees can be found by evaluating \(A(t)\) and \(B(t)\) at \(t = 0\):</p>
            <p>For forest \(A\):</p>
            <p>\( A(0) =   \displaystyle {@initial_A@}({@baseA@})^{0} = {@initial_A@} \cdot 1 = {@initial_A@} \)</p>
            <p>For forest \(B\):</p>
            <p>\( B(0) =   \displaystyle {@initial_B@}({@baseB@})^{0} = {@initial_B@} \cdot 1 = {@initial_B@} \)</p>
            <p>So, initially, forest \(A\) had {@initial_A@} trees, and forest \(B\) had {@initial_B@} trees. The difference is: \(  {@initial_difference@} \)</p>
                <p><strong>{@initial_trees@}</strong></p>
    	</li>

    	<li>
        	<p>Assuming the population growth models continue to represent the growth of the forests, which forest will have a greater number of trees after {@years@} years? By how many?</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> Give your answer rounded to the nearest whole number where necessary</p>
        	            <p>Evaluate \(A(t)\) and \(B(t)\) at \(t = {@years@}\):</p>
            <ol type="i">
                <li>
                    <p>For forest \(A\):</p>
            <p>\( A({@years@}) = {@initial_A@}({@baseA@})^{{@years@}}  ={@population_A_y@}\)  </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>For forest \(B\):</p>
            <p>\( B({@years@}) = {@initial_B@}({@baseB@})^{{@years@}}  ={@population_B_y@}\)  </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>The difference is: {@difference_y@}</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>Which forest will have a greater number of trees after {@years@} years?</p>
                <p><strong>{@years_growth@}</strong></p>
                </li>
            </ol>
    	</li>
	</ol>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
